WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Inferior Cranial Base: Foramina & Cranial Nerve Exit Topography.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The external base of the skull presents three zones containing critical foramina transmitting cranial nerves and vascular channels.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Foramen ovale transmits the mandibular nerve (V3), accessory meningeal artery, lesser petrosal nerve, and emissary veins (MALE).

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Foramen spinosum transmits the middle meningeal artery into the middle cranial fossa.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:01.000
The jugular foramen transmits CN IX (glossopharyngeal), CN X (vagus), CN XI (accessory), and the internal jugular vein.
